{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"1d5051a57c184937732c9067dee36ed8fcf0729a8ea33ff9dacb4607ffc4bfc5","slug":"midlatitude-cyclone-cyclogenesis","location":"/weather_technology/midlat_cyclone/midlatitude_cyclone_cyclogenesis.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Cyclogenesis Stage","content_includes_title":false,"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Kevin Goebbert","given":"Kevin","family":"Goebbert"},"name":"Kevin Goebbert","affiliations":["University of Tampa"],"id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"license":{"content":{"id":"CC-BY-4.0","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","name":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","note":"All non-code content is licensed under CC-BY-4.0","free":true,"CC":true},"code":{"id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://opensource.org/licenses/Apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","note":"All code content is licensed under Apache-2.0","free":true,"osi":true}},"github":"https://github.com/kgoebber/metpy_thebook","edit_url":null,"numbering":{"title":{"enabled":false,"offset":2},"equation":{"enabled":false},"figure":{"enabled":true,"continue":true}},"keywords":["metpy","python","meteorology","weather"],"copyright":"2026","affiliations":[{"id":"University of Tampa","name":"University of Tampa"}],"settings":{"output_stderr":"remove-warn","output_matplotlib_strings":"remove"},"source_url":"https://github.com/kgoebber/metpy_thebook/blob/main/weather_technology/midlat_cyclone/midlatitude_cyclone_cyclogenesis.md","thumbnail":"/metpy_thebook/_public/midlat_cyclone_cyclo-3540edc5285d8f12d4ae9bdeb2ea9506.png","thumbnailOptimized":"/metpy_thebook/_public/midlat_cyclone_cyclo-3540edc5285d8f12d4ae9bdeb2ea9506.webp","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"midlatitude_cyclone_cyclogenesis.md","url":"/metpy_thebook/_public/midlatitude_cyclone_-7113e62b1c870d82835881983363e895.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"For cyclogenesis to occur at the surface, a wave in the upper-levels\nmust come along to provide the necessary support to strengthen the\nlow-level temperature gradient. This stage is signified by an increasing\ntemperature gradient, the beginning of cyclonic flow at the surface, and\na small decrease in the mean sea-level pressure\n(","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"Zar6h9xmtl"},{"type":"crossReference","kind":"figure","identifier":"cyclogenesis","label":"cyclogenesis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fig. ","key":"UbVPx9EqbM"},{"type":"text","value":"26","key":"vphW6ClW5U"}],"template":"Figure %s","enumerator":"26","resolved":true,"html_id":"cyclogenesis","key":"RwXlY8jr4p"},{"type":"text","value":"). There are now\nfronts defined with a warm front typically east of the cyclone center\nand a cold front south and west of the cyclone center. The pressure\ntroughs in association with the fronts begin to develop.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"j2qGJmMDN5"}],"key":"bq7qbSXnve"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/metpy_thebook/_public/midlat_cyclone_cyclo-3540edc5285d8f12d4ae9bdeb2ea9506.png","alt":"Cyclogenesis stage of a Mid-latitude Cyclone","width":"650px","align":"center","key":"DJMfiPq43X","urlSource":"../../images/midlat_cyclone_cyclogenesis.png","urlOptimized":"/metpy_thebook/_public/midlat_cyclone_cyclo-3540edc5285d8f12d4ae9bdeb2ea9506.webp"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"captionNumber","kind":"figure","label":"cyclogenesis","identifier":"cyclogenesis","html_id":"cyclogenesis","enumerator":"26","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"t8btCuXSns"},{"type":"text","value":"26","key":"jFOIb4jv1f"},{"type":"text","value":":","key":"ynhtZMrLlK"}],"template":"Figure %s:","key":"eE8LuZ1oAe"},{"type":"text","value":"A schematic diagram of a surface cyclone during the cyclogenesis\nstage of development at the surface and 500 hPa with location of\nlow-level fronts for spatial reference.","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"RwWYJB2Ho1"}],"key":"SmVShJahW3"}],"key":"YfrOg1BStn"}],"label":"cyclogenesis","identifier":"cyclogenesis","enumerator":"26","html_id":"cyclogenesis","key":"UMOCwAXkKg"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":34,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"As the initial cyclone begins to develop, the trough begins to intensify\nsimultaneously. The intensification results from the different\ntemperature advection surrounding the mid-latitude cyclone. The 500-hPa\npattern strengthens (","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"EjNXPPHhFy"},{"type":"crossReference","kind":"figure","identifier":"cyclogenesis","label":"cyclogenesis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fig. ","key":"LfZXibqnCN"},{"type":"text","value":"26","key":"v2SRwnpacD"}],"template":"Figure %s","enumerator":"26","resolved":true,"html_id":"cyclogenesis","key":"C0NaXObTgz"},{"type":"text","value":") along\nwith the surface cyclone and is evidenced by the deepening of the\nupper-level trough. Additionally, a typical mid-latitude cyclone\nexhibits a tilt with height. The typical tilt is where the upper-level\ntrough (e.g., the 500-hPa trough) is located ","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"vaZZHsHxQY"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"to the west","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"wS9sPh6w1s"}],"key":"b7xBPXGnjD"},{"type":"text","value":" of the\nsurface mid-latitude cyclone (","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"b7rMAJhySO"},{"type":"crossReference","kind":"figure","identifier":"cyclogenesis","label":"cyclogenesis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fig. ","key":"jaSN2KO4Xy"},{"type":"text","value":"26","key":"oIsQyWtTKk"}],"template":"Figure %s","enumerator":"26","resolved":true,"html_id":"cyclogenesis","key":"iAeJTy031p"},{"type":"text","value":").\nThis ","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"sNuiWI2ed8"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"westward tilt","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"OesMIAvfbG"}],"key":"rot3BbMV0o"},{"type":"text","value":" with height is essential to the continued\nstrengthening of the mid-latitude cyclone.","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"SoMCc4G8qP"}],"key":"yilYowAEht"}],"key":"buoxSmotB1"}],"key":"N2cuMH9CjE"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Pre-Environment Stage","url":"/midlatitude-cyclone-pre-environment","group":"Introduction to Weather Technology using MetPy"},"next":{"title":"Mature Stage","url":"/midlatitude-cyclone-mature","group":"Introduction to Weather Technology using MetPy"}}},"domain":"http://pre.render"}